    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        290,
        990,
        1436,
        1350
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(a) The Committee shall be appointed by the Mayor and shall consist of nine members, including a Chair, each residing or having a principal place of business in the City of New York. The Committee Chair may, in his discretion designate adjunct members who shall function under section three as voting members with regard to appointments and reappointments to specific commissions, boards or other public bodies. Adjunct members, if so designated, shall have such expertise or knowledge as will assist the Committee in making a reasoned, informed and impartial evaluation of candidates for the offices referred to in section two. If so designated, there shall be, in the discretion of the Committee Chair, no more than four adjunct members for each commission board or other public body for which candidates are evaluated.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2462,
          "min": -1.3083
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0063,
          "min": -0.0125
        },
        "text": {
